desc: Loop Hole (4ms Dual Looping Delay port) by chmaha
tags: delay looper echo
author: chmaha
version: 1.1
changelog:
  Add full copyright and licence header (upstream authors' notices).
about:
  Two independent looping delays, A on the left channel and B on the right, each up to 87 seconds at 48 kHz.
  Time multiplies or divides the Ping period (x1 to x16, with the switch giving /8 or +16).
  Sync makes Ping one quarter note at the project tempo; with Sync off, tap the Ping button.
  Hold freezes the current loop, Reverse plays it backwards. MIDI notes 36/38 (Reverse A / Hold A)
  and 40/41 (Reverse B / Hold B) work like the module's trigger jacks.
  Ported from the 4ms Dual Looping Delay module of 4ms CoreModules (MetaModule / VCV Rack, 4ms Company,
  https://github.com/4ms/metamodule-core-modules, GPLv3+), original firmware by Dan Green (4ms Company).
  JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license
  Claude generated some of this code
